From 4c09563a1f00a05b6e9f8f5248cc0bcdec7dd12f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:33:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give every session an anticheat object instead of a null
 pointer

m_antiCheat is only ever assigned in InitAntiCheatSession, which WorldSocket
calls during a network login. Bot sessions are constructed directly with a
null socket and never pass through it, so for them the pointer stays null for
their whole life.

Seven call sites in MovementHandler dereference it without checking, and
PlayerbotAI.cpp:2035 calls HandleMoveKnockBackAck directly - one of them. Any
bot knocked back at the wrong moment takes the server down. Three more
unchecked uses sit in AsyncCommandHandlers.cpp and Creature.cpp.

The core already ships NullSessionAnticheat, a do-nothing implementation, so
every session now starts with one and InitAntiCheatSession swaps in the real
thing on login. That covers the unchecked sites without scattering null tests,
and the sites that already test the pointer keep working - they now see a
harmless object instead of nothing.

Found by comparing against Keyrosh021/tortoise-wow, which hit the knockback
crash and guarded the MovementHandler call sites individually.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/game/WorldSession.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/game/WorldSession.cpp b/src/game/WorldSession.cpp
index ef330da..a007cb2 100644
--- a/src/game/WorldSession.cpp
+++ b/src/game/WorldSession.cpp
@@ -101,6 +101,14 @@ WorldSession::WorldSession(uint32 id, WorldSocket *sock, AccountTypes sec, time_
     else
         m_Address = "<BOT>";
 
+    // Start every session with the null implementation so that m_antiCheat is
+    // never a null pointer. InitAntiCheatSession swaps in the real one during
+    // a network login; bot sessions never pass through WorldSocket and so had
+    // nothing at all. Several handlers dereference it without checking -
+    // HandleMoveKnockBackAck among them, which the playerbot module calls
+    // directly, so a knocked-back bot would take the server down.
+    m_antiCheat = std::make_unique<NullSessionAnticheat>(this);
+
     m_lastUpdateTime = WorldTimer::getMSTime();
     _analyser = std::make_unique<AccountAnalyser>(this);
 }
